+The default `redistributable` profile uses only the supplied fonts. It disables system-font scanning inside the temporary Docker container, verifies every input and generated font against a SHA-256-bound OFL-1.1 permission manifest, and emits `font-licenses.json` with the distribution. The manifest contains `fonts` entries with `file`, `sha256`, `license`, full `notice`, and an HTTPS `source`. Use input/output paths shared with Docker; staging is created beside the output.
+
+The legacy `zh-core` and `full` profiles must be selected explicitly. They can import fonts from the Docker image and do not establish redistribution rights. Do not publish their output as the reviewed `redistributable` distribution.
 
 ## Fixed `zh-core` Configuration
 
